body:
@stuartwdouglas right, but can we get it by default: one should be authenticated to access anything in the URI space of the application if we have an non-anonymous `SecurityIdentity` available ? 
IMHO we will not be too strict here, if some users need a semi-secured endpoint then let them do this extra configuration in application.properties or add `@Authenticated`. In this case it feels like a user has to express the intent twice, prepare OIDC (to get the user authenticated) and then do some more non-OIDC configuration to make this authentication effective.
What do you think ?
